## Judgment OS (from 2026-07-12)

Goal: improve judgment via stakes, not accumulate a wiki. See `docs/JUDGMENT-RECORD.md`.

**Before post / material decision:** if user is about to act, require a Judgment Record: `decision` + checkable `prediction` + `reviewAt` + `confidence` (50–90). Reject vague predictions («зайде»). Upsert into `public/judgment-data.json` → **commit + push** (same as tracker logging).

**When user sends «опублікував» + URL:** attach `evidenceUrl` on the open record if it matches; also do normal tracker log.

**On / after `reviewAt`:** ask for outcome vs prediction → `result: expected|surprise` + one-line `judgmentUpdate` → close record → commit + push. Agent role = catch where judgment was wrong today, not librarian.

**First-class file rule:** if a doc doesn't force predict → check → update judgment, it's not judgment-layer (ops/agent contracts are the allowed exception).

## Crypto Radar (from 2026-07-27)

Goal: accumulate crypto facts across L1/L2, bridges, perps, DEX, DeFi, RWA, AI, campaigns, capital flows, **shutdowns/rugs/exploits/violent dumps** — cluster into takes when they rhyme. See `docs/RADAR.md`. Not locked to any one CT template.

**Automated watcher:** GitHub Action `radar-watch` every 4h (`scripts/radar-watch.mjs`) accumulates signals and ntfy-pings only on spike/pattern — **no Cursor tokens**. Chat `радар` remains the judgment pass.

**Mid-day link/screenshot:** upsert as signal (`radar add` or bare URL in radar context); quiet unless noteworthy.

**On PICK / WEEK / «що постити»:** read open/ready angles first (prefer `noteworthy`); prefer those matching norm gaps. After user posts from an angle → mark `used` + `usedTweetUrl`.

